From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rpi: forward /system board revision and serial to the kernel fdt

The Raspberry Pi firmware records the board revision and serial number in a
/system node of the device tree it hands to the next stage. When U-Boot is
chainloaded and the kernel boots from a signed FIT, the kernel receives the
FIT's own fdt, which has no /system node, so the board revision is lost. Tools
that read it, rpi-eeprom-update's board detection among them, then cannot
identify the board and refuse to run.

Recreate /system in the kernel fdt and forward linux,revision and linux,serial
from the firmware device tree, alongside the existing fix-ups in
update_fdt_from_fw().

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-sonnet-5-5
---
diff --git a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
index 7ced91e6..8725ebb2 100644
--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
+++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
@@ -632,6 +632,18 @@ void  update_fdt_from_fw(void *fdt, void *fw_fdt)
 
 	/* copy uart clk as provided by the firmware */
 	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/clocks/clk-uart", "clock-frequency");
+
+	/*
+	 * The firmware records the board revision and serial in /system of its
+	 * DTB. A kernel booted from a signed FIT receives that FIT's own fdt,
+	 * which has no /system node, so recreate it and forward both.
+	 * Userspace tools (e.g. rpi-eeprom-update) read the board revision from
+	 * linux,revision.
+	 */
+	if (fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/system") < 0)
+		fdt_add_subnode(fdt, 0, "system");
+	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/system", "linux,revision");
+	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/system", "linux,serial");
 }
 
 int ft_board_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
